<title>BRAZIL: Aetna pumps $425 mln into Sul America deal.</title>
<headline>Aetna pumps $425 mln into Sul America deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. insurance giant Aetna Inc will pump $425 million into a joint venture with Brazil's largest private insurer Sul America Seguros, the head of Sul America said.</p>
<p>Aetna officials and Sul America president Rony de Castro Lyrio were in Brasilia to meet President Fernando Henrique Cardoso.</p>
<p>Sul America said last Friday it would make more details about the joint venture available at a news conference in Rio de Janeiro at 1530 local time/1730 GMT today.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
</text>
